HST Office: the crash handler ends even when the recovery UI cannot run.

Owner report (macOS 1.0.2 -> 1.0.3): the office was opened again while the updater replaced the app
bundle. The running 1.0.2 process then loaded a second libmergedlo.dylib from the new bundle, failed
on the 1.0.3 filter configuration and aborted. Inside the signal handler, Desktop::Exception created
the RecoveryUI service from that second copy, whose VCL was never initialised: SalInstance::
GetYieldMutex() read through a null instance and faulted on its first instruction. sal's handler
blocks every signal while it runs, so macOS re-executed the faulting instruction forever (sample:
1918/1918 at GetYieldMutex() + 0, 100 % CPU); only Force Quit ended it.

- Before the recovery UI, SIGSEGV, SIGBUS, SIGILL and SIGFPE get their default action back and are
  unblocked (POSIX only): a fault inside the recovery UI ends the process at once.
- A watchdog thread ends the process (_exit, EXITHELPER_FATAL_ERROR) when the recovery UI hangs:
  after 60 s in a row of a busy core, or after 10 minutes in any case. The emergency save dialog that
  waits for the user is idle, so it is not cut short; the autosaved recovery copies stay on disk.
- macOS: no recovery UI when the Info.plist of the bundle this process started from names another
  HST version (or is gone): the code loaded from then on and the recovery data cannot be trusted.
  Windows cannot replace the files of a running office (the installer closes it or asks for a
  restart); Linux has no single version file next to the program to compare, and the updater keeps
  a second office from starting while it installs.
--- a/desktop/source/app/app.cxx
+++ b/desktop/source/app/app.cxx
@@ -144,6 +144,17 @@
 #if defined MACOSX
 #include <errno.h>
 #include <sys/wait.h>
+#include <fcntl.h>
+#include <climits>
+#include <mach-o/dyld.h>
+#endif
+
+#include <cstring>
+#include <ctime>
+#include <string>
+#if !defined _WIN32 && !defined EMSCRIPTEN
+#include <pthread.h>
+#include <signal.h>
 #endif
 
 #ifdef _WIN32
@@ -1237,6 +1248,115 @@ bool lcl_flushConfigurationWithin(std::chrono::seconds aLimit)
     std::unique_lock aGuard(pState->aMutex);
     return pState->aDone.wait_for(aGuard, aLimit, [&pState] { return pState->bDone; });
 }
+
+// HST Office: the crash handler must end even when the recovery UI cannot run. On macOS an update
+// had replaced the app bundle under a running office; the second copy of libmergedlo it then loaded
+// created the RecoveryUI service, whose never-initialised VCL faulted on its first instruction. The
+// fault came inside the signal handler, where sal blocks every signal, so macOS restarted the
+// faulting instruction forever (100 % CPU, no window, Force Quit only).
+
+#if !ENABLE_WASM_STRIP_RECOVERYUI
+#if !defined _WIN32 && !defined EMSCRIPTEN
+// A fault inside the recovery UI ends the process at once (default action) instead of being blocked
+// and re-executed forever, or re-entering the handler that has nothing left to try.
+void lcl_makeNestedFaultsFatal()
+{
+    struct sigaction aDefault = {};
+    aDefault.sa_handler = SIG_DFL;
+    sigemptyset(&aDefault.sa_mask);
+    sigset_t aFaults;
+    sigemptyset(&aFaults);
+    for (int nSignal : { SIGSEGV, SIGBUS, SIGILL, SIGFPE })
+    {
+        sigaction(nSignal, &aDefault, nullptr);
+        sigaddset(&aFaults, nSignal);
+    }
+    pthread_sigmask(SIG_UNBLOCK, &aFaults, nullptr);
+}
+#endif
+
+// CPU seconds used by the whole process so far, or a negative value when unknown.
+double lcl_processCpuSeconds()
+{
+#ifdef _WIN32
+    FILETIME aCreation, aExit, aKernel, aUser;
+    if (!GetProcessTimes(GetCurrentProcess(), &aCreation, &aExit, &aKernel, &aUser))
+        return -1;
+    auto seconds = [](const FILETIME& rTime) {
+        return ((static_cast<unsigned long long>(rTime.dwHighDateTime) << 32) | rTime.dwLowDateTime)
+               / 1e7;
+    };
+    return seconds(aKernel) + seconds(aUser);
+#else
+    timespec aTime;
+    if (clock_gettime(CLOCK_PROCESS_CPUTIME_ID, &aTime) != 0)
+        return -1;
+    return aTime.tv_sec + aTime.tv_nsec / 1e9;
+#endif
+}
+
+// Ends the process from a second thread when the recovery UI hangs: after 60 s in a row of a busy
+// core (a loop: the emergency save dialog waiting for the user is idle), or after 10 minutes in any
+// case. The autosaved recovery copies stay on disk and are offered at the next start.
+void lcl_startRecoveryWatchdog()
+{
+    try
+    {
+        std::thread([] {
+            const auto aStart = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
+            int nBusySeconds = 0;
+            double fLast = lcl_processCpuSeconds();
+            for (;;)
+            {
+                std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::seconds(1));
+                const double fNow = lcl_processCpuSeconds();
+                nBusySeconds = (fLast >= 0 && fNow - fLast >= 0.9) ? nBusySeconds + 1 : 0;
+                fLast = fNow;
+                if (nBusySeconds >= 60
+                    || std::chrono::steady_clock::now() - aStart >= std::chrono::minutes(10))
+                    _exit(EXITHELPER_FATAL_ERROR);
+            }
+        }).detach();
+    }
+    catch (const std::system_error&)
+    {
+    }
+}
+#endif // !ENABLE_WASM_STRIP_RECOVERYUI
+
+#if defined MACOSX
+// True when the app bundle this process was started from now holds another HST version (an update
+// replaced it while this process ran) or is gone: code loaded from now on comes from another build,
+// and neither the recovery UI nor its data can be trusted.
+bool lcl_bundleReplaced()
+{
+    char aPath[PATH_MAX];
+    uint32_t nSize = sizeof aPath;
+    if (_NSGetExecutablePath(aPath, &nSize) != 0)
+        return false;
+    std::string sPlist(aPath);
+    const auto nMacOS = sPlist.rfind("/MacOS/");
+    if (nMacOS == std::string::npos)
+        return false;
+    sPlist.replace(nMacOS, std::string::npos, "/Info.plist");
+    const int nFile = ::open(sPlist.c_str(), O_RDONLY | O_CLOEXEC);
+    if (nFile < 0)
+        return errno == ENOENT;
+    std::string sText;
+    char aBuffer[16384];
+    ssize_t nRead;
+    while (sText.size() < 1024 * 1024 && (nRead = ::read(nFile, aBuffer, sizeof aBuffer)) > 0)
+        sText.append(aBuffer, nRead);
+    ::close(nFile);
+    const auto nKey = sText.find("<key>CFBundleShortVersionString</key>");
+    const auto nOpen = nKey == std::string::npos ? nKey : sText.find("<string>", nKey);
+    const auto nClose = nOpen == std::string::npos ? nOpen : sText.find("</string>", nOpen);
+    if (nClose == std::string::npos)
+        return false; // not the XML property list the build writes: unknown, keep the recovery
+    const auto nValue = nOpen + std::strlen("<string>");
+    return sText.compare(nValue, nClose - nValue, HST_VERSION) != 0;
+}
+#endif
 }
 
